---------- Forwarded message ----------

I am pleased to announce the release of GNU ddrescue 0.9.

GNU ddrescue is a data recovery tool.

The homepage is at http://www.gnu.org/software/ddrescue/ddrescue.html.

The sources can be dowloaded from http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/ddrescue/ or from your 
favorite GNU mirror.

The md5sum is:
f98e339818f2a81e28574baa5c8657a1  ddrescue-0.9.tar.bz2

This release is also GPG signed. You can download the signature by
appending ".sig" to the URL.

Changes in version 0.9:

* First release as part of the GNU project.
* Added configure script and info file.
* Two small bugs corrected.
* Added new option '--binary-prefixes' to show binary multipliers
   in numbers (SI prefixes are used by default).
* Numbers are accepted with decimal (SI) or binary multipliers.
* 'badblocks file' renamed to 'logfile'.
* Logfile is now also saved if max_errors are exceeded.


Please send bug reports and suggestions to <bug-ddrescue@gnu.org>.


Regards,
Antonio Diaz, GNU ddrescue author and maintainer.



